  "notes": "University Park. Verified 2026-08-27 against the CEE department's own real Civil Engineering Undergraduate Handbook (Fall 2025/Spring 2026, Rev #2, https://www.cee.psu.edu/assets/docs/handbooks/CE_undergrad_handbook.pdf), not just the bulletin. The bulletin's own 'Requirements for the Major' lists a 'CE 337 or CE 475' pick (1-4cr) as a separate item from the Suggested Academic Plan's unnamed 'CE Capstone Design' course in the final semester — modeled here as CE 337 (a real, concrete 1cr course) for the first requirement. The capstone slot now names the handbook's real 5 current capstone course codes (CE 439W is discontinued, replaced by CE 438W). Per the handbook's footnote 3, the 21 technical-elective credits split as 12cr CE/ENVE-locked ('CE Technical Elective', 4 slots) + 9cr broader-pool ('Technical Elective', 3 slots, handbook's approved department list) — corrected from an inverted 9/12 split. ENGL 202C is the only Additional Course the bulletin/handbook name for CE (no 202A/B/D equivalence documented for this major). CAS 100A/100B only (100C not listed for CE). Sem 3/4 Gen Ed and PHYS 212 swapped to match the real Suggested Academic Plan's Year 2 sequencing. 'etm' marks the gateway courses (Calc I, Physics I) everything downstream depends on. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair (unrelated to the handbook review, left largely as-is): CHEM 110's real catalog prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan, so MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) were added as an engine-only fallback chain for a hypothetical student with no reported math placement (see expand_math_placement in planner_engine.py) — target_credits values reflect the real bulletin per-semester load, not these bookkeeping-only items, which real students never actually take (satisfied instantly by the ALEKS/placement waiver in normal use). Removed 2026-08-27: this repair had also added MATH 3 and MATH 4 (Semester 1) on the theory that MATH 21 itself requires MATH 4 which requires MATH 3 — but math_catalog.json's own MATH 21 entry has an empty prereq_groups (no prerequisite at all), and MATH 3/MATH 4 are separately hardcoded as unconditionally-satisfied everywhere by expand_math_placement (planner_engine.py's NON_DEGREE_APPLICABLE_MATH) regardless of any student input. They were dead weight inflating the plan by 6 phantom credits with zero effect on schedulability (verified: build_full_plan produces identical zero-failure results with or without them for a no-placement-info student) — removed.",
